<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    Doctor-findings escalator.

    Runs unitares_doctor's operator-mode checks hourly and posts one
    fingerprinted finding per failing check, so the fleet's own detectors stop
    depending on a human remembering to run them.

    Why it exists: the doctor's live checks ran NOWHERE. No launchd job invoked
    it and CI imports it only for check_dockerfile_pinned_tags, a static check.
    Detectors for silent failure were themselves silent — Sentinel was
    governance-dark 24h from 2026-07-29 and Watcher was dead a month, and checks
    that would have caught both already existed.

    THIS DOCTOR NEVER HEALS. It diagnoses, escalates, and closes its own finding
    when the check returns to PASS.

    TWO ENVIRONMENT REQUIREMENTS, both load-bearing — do not drop them:

      PATH must include the dir that actually holds `psql`, which on Homebrew
      is NOT /opt/homebrew/bin. Nearly every operator check is DB-backed, and
      the doctor's _psql_row returns None — SKIP, not FAIL — when `psql` is
      absent, so a wrong PATH makes the whole sweep SKIP and report "all
      operator checks pass" forever.

      postgresql@17 is KEG-ONLY: brew does not symlink it into
      /opt/homebrew/bin, it stays at /opt/homebrew/opt/postgresql@17/bin.
      Shipping only /opt/homebrew/bin was the original bug here — verified
      2026-08-01, `ls /opt/homebrew/bin/psql` -> No such file, and the
      resulting --dry-run reported 8 of 11 checks SKIPPED. Confirm with
      `command -v psql` and put THAT directory first, rather than assuming.

      The version pin in the path is deliberate and self-announcing: if
      Postgres moves to @18 the sweep goes blind again, and doctor_sweep_blind
      is what tells you. Fixing PATH is the cure; the guard is only the net.

      python3 is PINNED to an interpreter that has the repo's DEPENDENCIES, not
      merely a new enough version. launchd's minimal PATH resolves python3 to
      /usr/bin/python3 (3.9.6) while the repo targets 3.12+ — but "3.12+" is
      not the whole requirement and reading it as such is how this broke.

      escalation imports agents.common.findings, which imports httpx at module
      level. A bare Homebrew python satisfies "3.12+" and still lacks httpx, so
      the sweep runs, diagnoses correctly, logs its findings — and every
      post_finding raises ModuleNotFoundError. Point this at a venv that has the
      project installed. Verify before trusting it:

        PYTHON_BIN -c "import httpx, sys; print(sys.version)"

      This is not hypothetical. com.unitares.deploy-drift-doctor ran hourly on
      /usr/bin/env python3 and posted ZERO findings across its entire life
      (verified 2026-08-01: no deploy_drift row in audit.events, ever) because
      its io_post_finding swallows the import error with `except Exception:
      pass`. It logged faithfully to a file nobody reads. Do not repeat that
      shape: if escalation cannot escalate, it must say so where someone looks.

    Before installing, substitute the placeholders:
      __UNITARES_ROOT__ -> absolute path to the deploy checkout
      PYTHON_BIN            -> absolute path to a 3.12+ interpreter

    Example:
      sed -e "s|__UNITARES_ROOT__|$HOME/projects/unitares-deploy|g" \
          -e "s|PYTHON_BIN|$(which python3)|g" \
          scripts/ops/com.unitares.doctor-findings.plist.template \
          > ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.unitares.doctor-findings.plist
      launchctl load ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.unitares.doctor-findings.plist

    Verify it can actually see the system (must NOT say "all operator checks
    pass" if the DB is reachable, and must NOT report doctor_sweep_blind):
      PYTHON_BIN scripts/ops/doctor_findings.py --dry-run

    Optional env:
      DOCTOR_FINDINGS_COOLDOWN  re-alert window per (check, status)
                                (default 21600 = 6h)
      DOCTOR_FINDINGS_SKIP      comma-separated checks to leave to other
                                watchdogs (default http_listening,http_health,pid_file)
      DOCTOR_FINDINGS_STATE     open/resolved state file
-->
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN"
  "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key><string>com.unitares.doctor-findings</string>
    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>PYTHON_BIN</string>
        <string>__UNITARES_ROOT__/scripts/ops/doctor_findings.py</string>
    </array>
    <key>WorkingDirectory</key><string>__UNITARES_ROOT__</string>
    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <key>PATH</key><string>/opt/homebrew/opt/postgresql@17/bin:/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
    </dict>
    <key>StartInterval</key><integer>3600</integer>
    <key>RunAtLoad</key><false/>
    <key>ProcessType</key><string>Background</string>
    <key>StandardOutPath</key><string>__UNITARES_ROOT__/data/logs/doctor-findings.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key><string>__UNITARES_ROOT__/data/logs/doctor-findings.err</string>
</dict>
</plist>
